WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.704
I'm Jimmy Fallon.
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.540
It's been a long and intense
week in this country,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.708
and I really do
appreciate you guys tuning in.

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:12.945
And I know a lot of
these conversations

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:16.883
are a little bit uncomfortable,
but they need to be had,

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.286
and we're having them and we're
going to continue to have them.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:24.524
So thank you again for joining
me in these conversations.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.125
I think we have a very
interesting and fun show

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.526
for you tonight.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:30.329
The Senator from the great state
of Vermont, Bernie Sanders,

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.298
is on the program this evening.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.700
Also, she's the head of
The King Center,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.369
the C.E.O. of The King Center.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.571
Her father is
Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.940
and her mom is
Coretta Scott King.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.144
Dr. Bernice King
is here tonight to talk to us.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.848
Also, the very funny Wyatt Cenac
is on the show.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.317
We'll close out the show with
a performance from

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.520
Gary Clark Jr. and The Roots.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.221
But, first,
let's get to some news.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.856
♪♪

00:00:57.856 --> 00:01:00.360
Well, guys, a former member of
President Trump's cabinet

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.929
is now speaking out against him.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.031
That could be like
one of 900 people,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.866
but this one happened to be his
former Defense Secretary,

00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:10.203
General James Mattis.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.338
In a statement,
General Mattis said,

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.275
"Donald Trump is the first
president in my lifetime

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.410
who does not try to unite
the American people,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.045
does not even pretend to try.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.648
Instead, he tries to divide us."

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.449
Trump saw that and was like,

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:27.053
"Why don't you be a man
and tweet that to my face?"

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.956
That's right -- Trump denied
he's trying to divide us.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:33.893
Then he added more fencing
between him and the protesters.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:37.062
By the way, in case anyone
forgot who General Mattis is,

00:01:37.062 --> 00:01:39.098
here's a photo.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:40.466
He looks like every
Scooby-Doo villain

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.369
who just had his mask
yanked off.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.106
Yep, several members of the
military are criticizing Trump.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.307
At this point,
the only military leaders

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.809
who support him are these guys.

00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:53.813
It's sad -- even his beloved
friend General Tso

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.515
has turned on him.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.283
Well, as the nation continues
to deal with

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.652
a pandemic and protests,
it seems like

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:03.222
the walls are closing in on
President Trump, literally.

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.691 line:0%
-President Trump beefing up
the physical barriers

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:07.593 line:0%
between himself
and between protesters.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.296 line:0%
Construction began before dawn
on some additional fencing

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.664 line:0%
for The White House complex.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.332
-I personally think the
fencing looks great.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:15.768
I always said, "I wish
The White House looked like

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.872
a Little League backstop."

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.640
I think the fence
would work well, too,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.977
unless protesters resort to
the act of pushing.

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.779
Yep, Trump is trying to protect
The White House.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.048
He even ran around putting
broken Christmas ornaments

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.917
under windows
and tying rope to paint cans

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:35.454
that swing over the staircase.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.823
"Keep the change,
you filthy animals."

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.892
So far, Trump has turned off
The White House lights,

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:41.393
hid in a bunker,
and is now building

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:43.529
an ugly chain-link fence.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:46.932
He's like every crazy neighbor
rolled into one.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:48.301
I think Trump has finally
had enough,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.969
'cause, yesterday he tweeted,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.805
"I've done more for black
Americans, in fact,

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.341
than any president
in U.S. history,

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.444
with the possible exception
of another Republican president,

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:02.314
the late, great Abraham Lincoln,
and it's not even close."

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:05.251
Yeah, with the possible
exception of Lincoln.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.552
Yeah, sure.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.221
He did -- I don't know what --
He did some things.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:12.124
But me first, then maybe
Lincoln did something.

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:14.193
But that is a real tweet,
and it makes me wonder.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.895
It's like, is there some
connection between

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.730
Trump and Lincoln that
I don't know?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.165
So I have right here --
I printed out

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:23.536
the actual text of Lincoln's
Gettysburg Address.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.705
And it turns out, the joke
is on me.

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:29.976
Here it is, from 1863,
the Gettysburg Address.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.411
[ Clears throat ]
♪♪

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:35.815 line:0%
"Four score and seven years ago,
our fathers --

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.883 line:0%
terrific people,
fantastic fathers --

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.119 line:0%
brought forth on this continent
a new nation

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.222 line:0%
conceived in liberty --
a beautiful thing, liberty --

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:44.723 line:0%
and dedicated to the proposition

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:46.525 line:0%
that all men are created equal.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:49.695 line:0%
The most equal.
Couldn't be more equal.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:51.997 line:0%
We were met on
the great battlefield --

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:53.199 line:0%
The great, classy field.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.334 line:0%
Everyone says
it's really classy.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.371 line:0%
And we're going to dedicate it
to those who gave their lives.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:01.607 line:0%
But, in a larger sense, we're
going to dedicate it to me.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.609 line:0%
We'll put up a sign,
a big, beautiful sign,

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:06.112 line:0%
that says "Lincoln Field"
in huge, gold letters

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:09.915 line:0%
with a golf course
and pro club and a cabana bar.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.151 line:0%
Now we are engaged
in a great civil war,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:15.321 line:0%
and it's very unfair how I've
been treated during this war.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.890 line:0%
The newspapers have not treated
Lincoln nicely.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.726 line:0%
They've said nasty things,
very nasty.

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.695 line:0%
You don't see them saying
those bad things about

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:26.098 line:0%
Sleepy General Sherman
or Creepy Custer.

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:27.934 line:0%
Sad!

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.337 line:0%
We here highly resolve that
this nation under God --

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.706 line:0%
great God, by the way,
good friend of mine --

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.275 line:0%
shall have a new birth
of freedom,

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:39.111 line:0%
especially when it comes to
the second amendment.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.814 line:0%
Everyone has the freedom
to fire a rifle,

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.983 line:0%
place a new bullet, from a
pouch, in the barrel,

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.885 line:0%
bite off the end of the
gunpowder pouch,

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.420 line:0%
take out a long stick,
shove all of that

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.455 line:0%
down the barrel, and fire again.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.690 line:0%
And if people want to fire as
many as one bullet

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.559 line:0%
every three minutes,
no government

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.462 line:0%
should be able to stop them,
not even the Lincoln government.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.465 line:0%
And that government of Lincoln,
by Lincoln, for Lincoln

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.367 line:0%
shall not perish from Earth.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:04.871 line:0%
Okay, if you need
me, I'll be in my bunker."

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.506 line:0%
Be best."

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.242
As if Trump isn't
dealing with enough,

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:13.179
now social-media companies
are starting to pile on.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.847 line:0%
-And we're learning right now
that Snapchat

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.283 line:0%
has apparently decided that
it's not gonna promote

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:19.485 line:0%
Donald Trump's pages,
saying that

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:22.588 line:0%
it's not gonna amplify voices
that incite racial violence.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.691
-When Trump heard the news,
he puked a rainbow.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.059
He was so mad.

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.794
He was like, "They didn't take
down my dance challenge

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.930
off TikTok, did they?"

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.798
Finally, you guys we've been in
quarantine for months,

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.034
and a lot of people are doing
a lot more online shopping

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.435
without even really thinking.

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:38.637
Well, I heard about this
new thing that you can download

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:41.273
that helps you put your money
towards organizations

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:42.474
that make a difference.

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:43.776
Check it out.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.278
-Are you a white person about to
buy some dumb crap online

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:47.780
to distract yourself right now?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.015
Has it occurred to you
that maybe

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.150
you could donate
that money instead?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.386 line:0%
You can, thanks to
Hmm...You Can Do Better,

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.322 line:0%
a new extension for Chrome
that takes the money

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.858 line:0%
you were going to spend
on useless crap you don't need

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.894 line:0%
and donates it to organizations
fighting for racial justice.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.362 line:0%
About to buy a canvas that says

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:06.466 line:0%
"Live, laugh, love,"
spelled out on seashells?

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.367 line:0%
You're gonna donate instead.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:12.304 line:0%
Thinking you might actually need
a Bluetooth avocado knife?

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:15.274 line:0%
Ya don't. Donate instead.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.009 line:0%
Considering a moon crystal
from your high-school friend

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.478 line:0%
Kaitlyn's
Facebook Marketplace page?

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:22.382 line:0%
Yeah, you're going to be
donating instead.

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:24.283 line:0%
Also, you should check
in on Kaitlyn.

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:26.819 line:0%
She's clearly caught up
in a pyramid scheme.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.288
Thanks to
Hmm...You Can Do Better,

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.924
you'll be turning your 3:00 a.m.
Ambien-induced shopping sprees

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.959
into social justice in no time.

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:35.561 line:0%
"But what if I want to
buy a candle

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:38.431 line:0%
shaped like a zebra
and donate?", you might ask.

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:41.667 line:0%
That's fine, but now you're
gonna donate twice, Carol.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.570 line:0%
And if you're finding it hard to
talk to your white relatives,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.273 line:0%
you can install the extension
on their computers, too,

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:50.176 line:0%
because Hmm...You Can Do Better
is now compatible with

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:53.412 line:0%
Yahoo!, AOL, and whatever
the hell me.com is.

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:55.014 line:0%
So next time
your cousin Todd tries to buy

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:58.017 line:0%
a 98-pound jug of protein powder
that physically cannot

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:00.052 line:0%
fit on any shelf and will sit on
his kitchen floor

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.921 line:0%
for three years,
we'll be sure to tell him,

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.189 line:0%
"Hmm...you can do better, Todd."

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:05.624 line:0%
Hmm...You Can Do Better --

00:07:05.624 --> 00:07:08.727 line:0%
together, we can turn your
bad taste into good action.

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.196 line:0%
Okay, I got to go donate.

